# Sites of tools/check/art7-loops.py in the release dex of an app (R8, and D8 --release), each judged:
# <class>.<method> | <owner>.<name> | <verdict> | <reason>. tools/check/art7-loops.py says what a site is and what each
# verdict means; docs/spec/art7-deopt-loops.md says why such a site can abort ART 7.x and how the triage was made. A site
# "inlined from" a callee is cached in that callee's profile: it is judged against every caller of the callee in the process.
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | kotlinx.coroutines.Deferred.isCompleted | one-class kotlinx.coroutines.CompletableDeferredImpl | conn.closed (H3Session.closed) and conn.quic.closed (ConnectionRuntime.closedDeferred) are both made by CompletableDeferred()
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | kotlinx.coroutines.Deferred.getCompleted | one-class kotlinx.coroutines.CompletableDeferredImpl | conn.closed (H3Session.closed) and conn.quic.closed (ConnectionRuntime.closedDeferred) are both made by CompletableDeferred()
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | kotlinx.coroutines.CompletableDeferred.isCompleted | one-class kotlinx.coroutines.CompletableDeferredImpl | inlined from ConnectionRuntime.isHandshakeComplete (every connection's handshake is made by CompletableDeferred()) and kotlinx's ReadonlyDeferred, which only asDeferred makes, over a CompletableDeferred: every caller in the process passes an Impl
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | kotlinx.coroutines.CompletableDeferred.isCancelled | one-class kotlinx.coroutines.CompletableDeferredImpl | inlined from ConnectionRuntime.isHandshakeComplete: every connection's handshake in the process is made by CompletableDeferred()
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicReferenceFieldUpdater.get | one-class java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicReferenceFieldUpdater$AtomicReferenceFieldUpdaterImpl | inlined from kotlinx's JobSupport.state: one static updater shared by every job of the process, the framework's one implementation
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | io.kuicksilver.quic.QuicConnection.getClosed | one-class io.kuicksilver.quic.runtime.ConnectionRuntime | conn.quic is the pool's own QUIC connection: ConnectionRuntime is the one QuicConnection the library makes, and an app's own never reaches the pool
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | io.kuicksilver.quic.QuicConnection.isHandshakeComplete | one-class io.kuicksilver.quic.runtime.ConnectionRuntime | conn.quic is the pool's own QUIC connection: ConnectionRuntime is the one QuicConnection the library makes
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | kotlinx.coroutines.flow.StateFlow.getValue | one-class kotlinx.coroutines.flow.StateFlowImpl | conn.goAwayReceived is H3Session's val made by MutableStateFlow()
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | java.util.Set.contains | one-class java.util.LinkedHashSet | retryOffered holds a LinkedHashSet from the start, and + and - make LinkedHashSets: one class at `conn in retryOffered.load()`
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | kotlinx.coroutines.sync.Mutex.lock | one-class kotlinx.coroutines.sync.MutexImpl | the pool's lock is a val made by Mutex()
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | kotlinx.coroutines.sync.Mutex.unlock | one-class kotlinx.coroutines.sync.MutexImpl | the pool's lock is a val made by Mutex()
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | kotlinx.coroutines.sync.MutexImpl.tryLock | one-class kotlinx.coroutines.sync.MutexImpl | inlined from MutexImpl.lock on `this`: every caller in the process locks a MutexImpl, which nothing subclasses
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | java.util.HashMap.get | one-class java.util.HashMap | connections is a val made by HashMap(), never a LinkedHashMap
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | java.util.HashMap.remove | one-class java.util.HashMap | connections is a val made by HashMap(), never a LinkedHashMap
io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.h3.H3Pool.execute | java.util.HashMap.entrySet | one-class java.util.HashMap | connections.entries on a 421: connections is a val made by HashMap(), never a LinkedHashMap
